From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0081] anv: Xe2 encodes AV1 up to 8K: multi-tile frames and multi-tile HuC BRC

On top of fac3fc75 (a3ad934 + 0074 0075 0048 0049 0076 0077 0078 0079 0080).

- Caps: AV1 encode maxCodedExtent 8192x8192 and maxLevel 6.3 on Xe2, as media-driver
  (capstable_data_av1_encode_xe2_hpm_r0_specific.h: VAConfigAttribMaxPictureWidth/Height = CODEC_8K_MAX_PIC_*);
  was 4096 / level 5.3.
- Buffers: the VDEnc intra row store, tile row store and cumulative CU count streamout are sized from the session's
  max coded extent (at least 4096, so <= 4K sessions keep their layout); the AVP buffers already were (0074).
- Tiles: a frame wider than 4096 needs at least two tile columns, and 8K at least 2x2 tiles (AV1 5.9.15
  MAX_TILE_WIDTH / MAX_TILE_AREA). FFmpeg passes no pTileInfo, so the frame header writer (vk_video) and ANV both take
  the minimum the frame size imposes (vk_video_av1_uniform_tiles_log2), and the header codes the increments over it.
- VDENC_CMD2 TilingEnable now follows the tiles the frame is coded with (media-driver Av1BasicFeature VDENC_CMD2:
  tile_cols > 1 || tile_rows > 1), not pTileInfo: a 4-tile frame with TilingEnable clear hung the VDBox (GuC reset).
- HuC BRC with more than one tile (one tile group, single pipe), as media-driver Av1BrcUpdatePkt::
  AddAvpPicStateBaseOnTile / Av1VdencPktXe2_Hpm::AddOneTileCommands: a second AVP_PIC_STATE (no header) right after
  the first in the SLBB, UPD_AVPPiCStateCmdNum 2 and UPD_TileNum = tiles; the tiles after the first execute it.
  Was: BRC only for single tile frames.
- The tile group obu_size with BRC header variants and more than one tile: one leb128 per variant (the payload is the
  frame's bytes past that variant's header), computed outside the small variant batches.

Single-tile streams are byte-identical to fac3fc75 (4K 8-bit VBR, 1080p 10-bit VBR, CQP).

